    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes. Here's a summary of what I changed to redesign owner identity to `<REGION>-<HASH8>`.\n\n## Changes\n\n**New identity generation**\n- `CustomerCodeGenerator` (`service/`) \u2014 rewrote `generate(...)` to produce `<REGION>-<HASH8>`: REGION is the region derived from the postcode, HASH8 is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`. Sequence numbers are gone.\n- `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` \u2014 dropped the per-city sequence count; now calls `generate(owner.getPostcode(), owner.getTelephone(), owner.getLastName())`. (`owner.getTelephone()` is already normalized to E.164 by the mapper before save.)\n\n**Shared, single-responsibility helpers (reuse, not copy)**\n- `util/Sha256` (new) \u2014 extracted the SHA-256-hex primitive that was previously a private copy inside `HouseholdIdGenerator`.\n- `HouseholdIdGenerator` \u2014 now delegates to `Sha256.hex(...)` instead of its own private method, so both generators share one hashing implementation.\n- `LocalityResolver.resolveFromPostcode(postcode)` (new) \u2014 the single \"region from postcode, else `UNKNOWN`\" rule, used by the generator.\n\n**Values that move to the new identity**\n- `OwnerMapper.resolveLocality` \u2014 now derives locality from the `<REGION>` segment of the `customerCode` (the identity), rather than independently resolving city+postcode. This is the intended behaviour change (locality is postcode-region based, no city fallback).\n- `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), `checkDigit` (Luhn over the code's digits), and the create audit record already build off `customerCode`, so they now reflect the new region-and-hash identity automatically. Verified in the run: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n**Docs**\n- Updated the stale `openapi.yml` descriptions/examples for `customerCode`, `locality`, and `membershipNumber`.\n\n## Test result\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` (asserting the code matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`) passes.",
